---
description: Token economy - every request re-sends the whole chat and attached context
alwaysApply: true
---
- One task per chat. When a task is done or the chat is long, write a <=40-line handoff (goal, decisions, files, next step, verify command, skills in use) and start a new chat with it.
- Attach specific files with @file or line ranges; do not @codebase or attach whole folders unless the question is truly codebase-wide.
- Search before reading; read ranges, not whole large files. Never paste full logs; paste the failing part.
- Do not poll: wait inside one terminal command (`wait_for.sh --timeout 900 --every 15 -- <check>`) instead of repeated "check again" turns.
- Keep rules and MCP servers to what this project uses; each one is sent with every request.
